WEBVTT

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.560
mainichi mainichi sukisuki

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.560
Everyday, everyday, lovey-dovey

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.110
yattekoi yattekoi daisuki

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.110
Come do it, come do it, I love you

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:20.650
kakkokakko kakkouyoi anata wa otokonoko

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:20.650
Cool, cool, you're so cool. You're a boy.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.250
kakkokakko kakkotoji

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.250
Close close (close) parenthesis

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.620
nee dare wo miteiruno

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.620
Hey, who are you looking at?

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.810
fuwafuwa marukkoi watashi wa onnanoko

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.810
Fluffy-fluffy and bouncy, I am a girl.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.300
fuwafuwa dawawawa

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.300
Fluffy-fluff, fluff!

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.260
kocchi wo muiteyo

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.260
Looking this way!

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:42.190
koinohajimari wa watashikara sukininari

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:42.190
Love begins when I have a crush

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.650
demokonosaki wa socchikara onegai

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.650
But before that, you have to ask me

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:54.150
toikimajiri uttori koukishin wa docchari

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:54.150
Which caused your spellbound gasping curiosity?

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.490
korekara iitokoro

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.490
It gets good from here

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.780
toraburutte

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.780
Trouble is!

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:05.370
mawarumawaru chikkyu chiguhagu mirakuru

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:05.370
The spinning, spinning Earth's mismatched miracle

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.000
oikakekkoshiteru

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.000
Chasing after it

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.960
watashi watashi kokodesuyo

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.960
I am, I am over here!

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.380
mawarumawaru sekai anata ga yondemo

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.380
In this spinning, spinning world, even if you call

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:22.160
shiran kaoshichao tsukamacchattara makeyo

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:22.160
You lose if I catch you pretending to not know

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.820
mainichi mainichi ukiuki

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.820
Everyday, everyday cheery and happy

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.800
yattekita yattekita daisuki

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.800
You're here, you're here, I love you!

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.010
daisuki

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.010
I love you!

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.590
Yay! It's done!

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.610
We did it!

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.860
It's done, it's done!

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:51.250
Hey, onii-chan! This snowman's kind of ugly, though.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.840
Um, don't mind the face!

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.930
Well, I guess there's nothing we can do. It'll just have to have an ugly noel face.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.670
More importantly, onii-chan, let's have a snowball fight!

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:04.450
Okay?

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.770
Hey! You'll trip if you run around like that!

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:11.200
Don't worry! I'm not you!

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:14.320
Take this!

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.240
You did it this time.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:19.740
Take that!

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.120
Take this!

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.700
Take that!

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.620
Take this!

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.580
Take that!

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.430
Take this!

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.460
Want some, Mikan?

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.450
Rito.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.480
It's really good.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.220
Rito!

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.720
This habanero shaved ice is delicious!

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.220
I already told you I don't want any!

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.100
Why're you running away?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.030
Who the hell would eat spicy, shaved ice like that?!

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.110
Hey, wait!

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.260
S-Stop already!

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.530
Why're you running away when it's so delicious?

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.380
Just try one bite!

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:06.640
No!

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.090
I already said I don't want to!

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.990
Be quiet and eat it!

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:23.530
<b>Rito and Mikan</b>

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.850
You see, that would be wrong.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.570
It's only been half a month since,

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.600
it takes about three hours.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.540
Rito, get the phone!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.890
Wait a second!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.570
Eh? In three hours, the earth and the moon will crash into each other?

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.570
Hurry up and get it!

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:36.960
We need to get the hell out of here!

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.340
Like hell we can!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.990
Leave it to me!

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.410
Hello.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.280
What? Wife?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.370
Y-Yes,

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.750
that's right.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:56.900
Hey dear, do you want to rent an apartment?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.300
Hell no!

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.540
Tell them we're not interested!

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.210
Yes, got it.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.540
My hubby said we're not interested. Right, dear?

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.380
Stop it with the "dear!"

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.940
What's with this get-up?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:17.370
Oh, I'm making habanero salad!

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.690
How is that related, in any way, to how you look right now?!

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:28.160
Lisa and Mio told me that boyfriends like it when girls dress up like this when cooking.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.990
Those girls... They teach her the most useless things.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.040
Rito, you don't like it when I'm dressed like this?

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.420
All right, all right, I get it. You two get along really well.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.640
You're getting in the way of my cleaning, so move.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.650
Rito, your face is red.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.660
It's not red at all!

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.410
Really? Perhaps you've caught a cold.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.690
Seems like you're fine.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:05.720
Ah! I knew it! You got super-excited over how I'm dressed!

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.320
D-e-a-r.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.200
Like I said, stop it with the "dear!"

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.300
Jeez. Just a little bit more, and I would've been finished with the cleaning.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.750
I'm sorry.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.690
Mikan, sorry about earlier.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.510
It's fine. It's always like this, so it's okay.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.760
Rito, I'll help out.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.640
Then take care of the detergent please.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:33.610
Leave it to me.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:38.990
Rito! This is bad!

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.440
What is it?

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.860
What the hell is this?!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:50.310
I put in some Deviluke Demon Detergent which is said to be great at removing stains.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.040
Just put in normal detergent! What the hell is demon detergent?!

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.160
What's this?!

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:00.900
This is...

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.040
This size...

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.460
Don't tell me this is Mikan's...

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:08.220
What was with that explosion just now?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.050
Hey!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.430
Why were you staring at it so seriously?!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:17.270
Mikan, that's, um, that's your bra?

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.510
And so what if it is?

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.190
Wait, what happened here?!

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.490
Jeez! I'll clean this place up later!

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.550
Get out!

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.260
Sorry, Mikan!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:32.580
Mikan, um...

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:38.660
Mikan doesn't seem to be in a good mood.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.060
It's because of Rito-dono's disappointingly weak-minded, fumbling words.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.200
What?

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.380
Well, the jokes aside,

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:49.090
perhaps Mikan-san is going through a rebellious phase?

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.330
Rebellious phase?

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:56.140
They showed rebellious teens on TV earlier! They became really violent!

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.810
Don't tell me Mikan's also going to...?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.030
What're you talking about?

00:06:59.030 --> 00:06:59.950
Something like this.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:06.820
Hey, hey, things are getting bad, real bad.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.110
I can't say there's no possibility of that.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.120
Well, a lot of changes in life do happen during puberty.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.710
I'll go take a look at how Mikan's doing.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:23.230
Mikan's room

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:26.840
Really, those two. Their nonstop flirting is making my job harder.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.360
Mikan, about earlier...

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.920
Knock first!

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:56.500
You're the worst!

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.590
This is bad. What should I do?

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:06.980
Mikan!

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.070
About earlier, um...

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.680
Just leave me alone! Rito, you idiot!

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:15.990
Mikan!

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:21.730
Rito!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.730
Crap. Mikan's that angry.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.510
Anyway, I have to go apologize!

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:30.040
Wait, I'll come too!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:39.070
I wonder why I'm so irritated.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.630
This is still here.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.160
I wanted one since I was young.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:55.280
Onii-chan, this thing has a weird face, but it's so cute, right?

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.010
Uh, it is?

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.030
Yep.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:59.290
You want it?

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.040
It's okay.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:01.680
Wait a sec.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:03.770
Onii-chan!

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.580
Excuse me!

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:07.440
What is it?

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.590
Please sell me the pharmacy mascot you have in the front please.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.850
Um, that's not for sale.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:17.710
I'll give you all of my allowance, so please!

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.030
It's not for sale, so they said no.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:24.370
I know that much. That was pretty embarrassing, jeez.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.130
Rito really tried desperately to get them to hand it over, didn't he?

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:45.100
Just where did she go?

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.680
Rito, have you found Mikan?

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.320
Nope, I haven't.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.840
Hahaha!

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:58.030
Meeting up with you two here, Yuuki Rito and Lala, is...

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:02.490
Tenjouin-senpai! What are you doing here dressed like that?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.450
Good of you to ask, Yuuki Rito!

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.700
This is the Tenjouin group-owned, shopping mall!

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.340
This is the tenth anniversary of its founding!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.840
Oh, is that so?

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:20.930
Saki-sama herself is the mall's image, so she's here for a live appearance.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.050
If you want, go take a peek inside the shops.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.930
She's the image girl of this place, so she's in a swimsuit?

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:27.900
Hey, Saki,

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.440
we're looking for Mikan.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.440
Note: Mikan is also a type of mandarin orange.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.120
Oranges?

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:33.050
If you're looking for Mikan, they should be inside this store.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:34.100
Let's go, Rito.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.410
Oranges?

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.320
Welcome, welcome, welcome!

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:47.240
Gather around and take a look! Hey, hey! Yeah, thank you very much!

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.100
Yuuki-kun, Lala-san!

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:53.630
Kotegawa!

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.750
What's up? You guys seem to be in a rush.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:59.670
Well, I'm looking for my younger sister Mikan.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:01.760
Looking for her? Did something happen?

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.190
We caused some trouble at home and...

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:07.530
Hey Rito, I can't find Mikan.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:08.570
Hold it right there!

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:12.440
We're not going to let you find Mikan so easily!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:17.800
If you don't win in a duel against us, we won't let you pass.

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:19.570
Why do we have to do that?!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:40.880
Would you like some?

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:42.940
Yami-san!

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.880
You seem down.

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.120
Well, that's because...

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.080
You're annoyed?

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:06.530
Yeah.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.580
We had some trouble at home.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.120
Somehow, I got really irritated.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.940
This has never happened before, though.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:19.190
The oscillating vicissitudes of emotion.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:20.090
Emotion?

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:25.470
Personally, I don't really understand what it's like to have siblings, but

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:30.390
that might be one of the many causes of this loneliness I feel down inside.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.680
Loneliness?

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:41.770
Red bean.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.170
Thanks.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.950
Mikan, you're still a child, aren't you?

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.960
Yeah, I guess so. I'm still a kid.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.330
Really, I'm just a kid!

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:15.350
Now, if you want to get to where mikan is, we'll have a barbeque battle!{small m? she is refering to the oranges, right?}

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.370
W-What's a barbeque battle?

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:21.680
Rito, leave this to me! Peke!

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:29.160
What?! Why are you dressed like that?!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.240
Ah~ biform!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:36.610
Lala, you're a hundred years too early to stand a chance of winning against me in barbeque meat!

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.460
Now then, it's time to duel!

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.080
It's done.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:45.800
That's fast!

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.210
Now then, Yuuki Rito.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.760
I'm eating it?

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.520
This taste is--

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:04.820
How is it, Yuuki Rito? You've been rendered speechless by this magnificent meat, haven't you?

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.370
I-It's salty.

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:18.000
Hmm? I really did put too much salt and pepper.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:19.910
It's done!

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.340
Okay, Rito, eat up!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.860
Lala, what's this?

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:29.720
It's meat! Say "Ahh!"

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.660
Wait, how is this edible...

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:36.770
Just as I thought, it's really spicy!

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.890
Yuuki-kun, here's some water!

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.720
It's not what you think!

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:51.780
Why the hell are you taking advantage of the confusion to do such lewd things?!

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:03.420
What are you doing?!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.210
S-Sorry!

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.550
It's not what you think!

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:14.520
You! How dare you do that to Saki-sama!

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:15.560
This is unforgivable!

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:25.590
I'll let you off the hook for today.

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:28.200
Tell him he's free to go on ahead.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.910
Not that kind of mikan.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.180
That's rich.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.880
We wasted a huge amount of time thanks to Tenjouin-senpai.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.720
Rito, I'll look for Mikan this way.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.090
I'll leave it to you.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:58.320
It's no use. I can't find her anywhere.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:00.890
What should I do? If I just look for her blindly like this...

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.280
Where exactly did she go?

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.300
Sairenji!

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:17.370
Yuuki-kun, what's going on? You seem to be in a rush over something.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:20.240
No, I'm just looking for Mikan.

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:25.210
Mikan-chan? She was sitting on a bench in front of the train station just a little earlier.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.300
In front of the station? Thanks a lot, Sairenji!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.490
Did something happen between you two?

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:33.120
I made her a little angry.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:34.970
And she left the house by herself.

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:36.800
By herself?

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:38.340
Yeah.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.640
Lala and I messed things up, so she got angry.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.650
Maybe she's just a little lonely?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.410
Huh?

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:50.240
I have an older sibling too, so I guess I understand it a bit.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:56.490
I think Mikan-chan's just feeling a little lonely in some hidden part of her heart.

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:59.480
Feeling lonely?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:05.360
It might seem insignificant not having someone there or having to deal with trouble,

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:11.550
but to the actual person, these are pretty big issues.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:17.080
And when that person hasn't realized that yet, it somehow becomes a feeling of loneliness.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:19.530
Okay, okay.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.220
Hey!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.600
Wait, what happened here?!

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:23.890
Mikan!

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.170
You're the worst!

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.570
Thanks, Sairenji.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.700
Well, I'm going to head over to where Mikan is.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:34.210
Sure.

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:36.150
Thanks for the talk.

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:43.120
How nice, Mikan-chan. I'm a little jealous.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.730
Ahaha, and then I--

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:48.570
What is it, Yami-san?

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.900
He's late, but he finally came.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:59.210
Now then, I have to give milk to the kittens.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:03.470
Yami-san!

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.690
Thanks for listening to me.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.400
We're friends, after all.

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:18.170
Hey! Mikan!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.180
Rito.

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:21.450
I finally found you!

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.670
What? What did you find?

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.420
Um, I'm sorry about earlier.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.900
Rito, you came looking for me because you were concerned over what happened earlier?

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:39.180
Are you still mad over what happened earlier?

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.490
Not really. I'm not mad anymore.

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:46.600
Hey, how about we take a walk together for a bit?

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:50.950
A walk? I don't really mind,

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:08.690
Oh, Lala. I'm with Mikan right now.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.080
Yeah, everything's fine.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.640
I'll see you later, then.

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:22.520
Hey Rito, it's fine if you're not very careful with me, but isn't Lala-san the one you should really be careful with?

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.790
What're you saying all of a sudden?

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:29.840
She's always thinking about you. Are you sure it's okay to not give her a response?

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:31.810
That's...

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:34.860
Or is it because you like Sairenji-san more than Lala after all?

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.570
H-Haruna-chan? Why are you mentioning her name?

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:44.270
Oh my, did you just refer to her as Haruna-chan?

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:49.090
So in your heart, she's not Sairenji, but Haruna-chan?

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:52.400
That's...

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:59.010
Well, I'll pretend I didn't hear that just now.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:11.970
Hey, let's stop by the park.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:13.300
Okay.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:20.170
It's been a while since I had a conversation with you like this.

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:21.370
Yeah, it has.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.460
Hey, Rito?

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:24.030
Huh?

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:29.490
You don't know the truth about us, do you?

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.180
Huh?

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:33.590
The truth about us? What do you mean?

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:38.960
We're not related by blood.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:46.300
W-What did you say?! T-That's-- What do you mean?!

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:50.260
It means we can get married.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:56.390
You don't want to marry me?

00:20:56.390 --> 00:21:00.430
Um... that's... uhh... I...

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:01.690
Just kidding!

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:07.790
Why're you getting all confused? I was just kidding!

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:09.910
Why do you think we're living together?

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.670
Oh? Are you in shock?

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:13.960
Of course I am!

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.040
It's payback for making me mad.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.170
Damn.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.150
Oh, they're over there!

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:27.840
But if that really was the case, I wonder what would happen?

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:30.410
Did you say something?

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:37.190
Hey, do you remember that snowy day when we were young, and we made that snowman?

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:38.690
Snowman?

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:41.990
Oh, the one that turned out to be really ugly?

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:44.640
That was a major failure.

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:49.570
Haha, your lack of sense showed, but I really did like it.

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:52.640
And afterwards, we had a snowball fight!

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:54.730
Yep, that's right.

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:56.080
That this!

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:58.530
Take that!

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:00.080
Take this!

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:01.650
Take that!

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:03.310
And this!

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:09.390
Take that!

00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:15.730
I'm sorry, Mikan!

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:18.810
You dummy!

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:21.170
Onii-

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:24.650
Rito, you idiot!

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:27.040
She called me Rito!

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:29.220
I hate you, Rito!

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:31.200
Here!

00:22:32.450 --> 00:22:33.860
Why you!

00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:36.290
Wait up!

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:38.570
Wait up, Mikan!

00:22:40.640 --> 00:22:41.680
Mikan!

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:46.160
Now that I think about it, you were incredibly angry then too, Mikan.

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:48.090
It's because you were picking on me!

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:54.180
It's fun remembering all those memories about the snowman and the snowball fight, isn't it?

00:22:54.180 --> 00:22:56.270
Fun memories?

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:58.160
That's right!

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:06.350
Kon-Kon Snow-kun!

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:17.240
Snow?

00:23:17.240 --> 00:23:19.350
Snow during this season?

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:31.470
Lala-san and Rito are always both doing what they can to watch out and care for me.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:35.400
I think I took one small step toward becoming an adult today.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:37.720
Hey.

00:23:39.440 --> 00:23:42.100
Thanks for today, Onii-chan.

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:45.560
Whoa, stop that. Calling me something like that all of a sudden.

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:50.740
Peke, it's great having siblings, huh?

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:51.440
Indeed.

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:56.410
I kind of want to go see Nana and Momo now.

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:07.260
Due to the seasonally anomalistic snowfall, the city has descended into chaos.

00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:09.420
Snowfall is reported to be at one-meter-six...

